+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+Tool calls are checked against the JSON Schema declared by the resolved tool definition before an executor receives them. Invalid input is reported as a tool result so the model can correct the call, while unknown tool names remain exceptional.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required fields and wrong-typed fields with a result naming the failing field and constraint, without invoking the executor or exposing the offending value ([validated by: returns schema failures with the field and expected type without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17)).
+- Valid input, including unlisted extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged exactly once, while an unregistered name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: passes valid extra properties through unchanged exactly once and preserves unknown-tool errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A static schema is compiled once at registration, an uncompilable schema names its tool in the registration error, and a function-valued definition is validated against the schema resolved for that call ([validated by: compiles static schemas once, rejects an uncompilable schema at registration, and validates dynamic schemas per call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L51)).
